/-!
# Economics and Mathematical Formalism

This module records the formalization scope for
`1 - theoretical foundations/1_economics.tex`.

The chapter contains the three guiding principles of the framework rather than
technical lemmas:

* `prin:agent-actions`: agents may take any action allowed by resources and
  legislation.
* `prin:finitism`: over finite time intervals, realized agents/actions are
  finite.
* `prin:clearing`: a market is cleared exactly when no admissible exchange
  remains that the involved agents jointly want to execute.

These principles are kept as commentary for now. Later chapters formalize their
mathematical consequences through finite tuple spaces, market actions, and
clearing operators.
-/

